  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Fedora's CLI utilities should be reworked so that:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "We use one client library throughout (and stop using the old FedoraClient)",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Batch operations are supported throughout",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This can be accomplished a variety of ways.  Here's a proposal:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A) We use Kai's fedora-cli project as a replacement for the existing client batch/shell scripts.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "B) Kai's fedora-cli project uses the new MediaShelf-developed java Fedora Client",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "C) Batch operations become scripts passed to fedora-cli.  This would subsume the existing batchmodify functionality, and support the batch purge use case highlighted in ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-756#icft=FCREPO-756"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
